#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tenure — a path-condition occupies history.

`when` answers, at one snapshot: which nested predicates are in force
at FILE:LINE. `perch` answers: eras where a user-supplied predicate
(grep/exists/exec) is true, split again when the witness set changes.

Those two piped (`when | held`) grep the if-text. The if-text lives on
the guard line; occupancy of a path-condition is the lines that *run
under* the stack. tenure walks git history, reconstructs stacks, and
emits eras of “this stack held” plus who sat in it.

The condition frames are the predicate. The functions/files/regions
that currently have a line in that stack are the holders. Same TRUE,
different occupants → a new era. `--boolean` downcasts to held.
"""

